# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
# Root-level Python build output ONLY — note the leading slash, and do not remove it.
#
# This was a bare `build/` until v0.2.9. A bare rule matches at every depth, so it also
# swallowed this site's own build tooling: admin/build/ (chrome.py, validate.js,
# version.txt) and governance/build/ (build.py, floor.py, gates.py). Neither is Python
# build output.
#
# admin/build/ was caught at v0.1.0, when CI failed with MODULE_NOT_FOUND, and was fixed
# by re-including that one path by name. governance/build/ was NOT — it was created at
# v0.2.6 and shipped unversioned through v0.2.7 and v0.2.8, because the generated HTML
# was committed and the generator that produced it was silently dropped every time. It
# surfaced only when a debrief linked to floor.py on GitHub and the link 404'd.
#
# Fixing the instance a second time would have guaranteed a third. Anchoring the rule to
# the repository root fixes the class: no `<section>/build/` can be swallowed again, and
# the by-name re-includes admin/build/ needed are no longer required.
/build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
#   Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#   before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec

